[{:seon.task/name "staging-unmaps-only-what-the-runtime-unmapped"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by step E's dry run (2026-10-22, worktree dry-run; notes dry-run-merge-revert.md): `seon.stage/stage-tx` retracts every var recorded on the branch with a form whose namespace is loaded and which is not interned there, reading it as an unmap. A form the agent's runtime never loaded is not an unmap: on the dry run, two seon.lib-test vars imported at boot but never loaded (`seon.program/held?` then read a loaded namespace as the binary's own; fixed on jolt/dry-run) were retracted by the merge agent's `my.branch/merge-main!` (which harvests first), and the merge deleted them from main and from the written-back file. The held? fix removes that path, but any form that fails to load in an agent (an eval error at load-changes!, a load the agent skipped) is still deleted from main at its next merge. Correct: staging retracts only what the runtime unmapped: a var that was bound when the agent was forked (or that the agent itself defined) and is no longer interned; a var never bound in this runtime is left as main has it. Proof: on a branch whose db records a var the runtime never bound, `seon.stage/stage-tx` answers no retraction of it; a var the agent unmapped with `ns-unmap` is still retracted."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.stage-test/a-var-the-runtime-never-bound-is-not-unmapped}}]
